# Quickstart

Read the switch from your MCU: wire three signals, write a small port class, call two driver functions.

## 1. Wire it

| MCU | XMPL100 | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| GPIO input | OUT | Pull-up to 3.3 V (10 kΩ, or the MCU's internal one) |
| 3.3 V | VDD | 100 nF to GND close to the pin |
| GND | GND | |

## 2. Add the driver

```bash
git submodule add https://github.com/kokeb-labs/driver-template.git external/driver-template
```

